{"kind":"driver:amendment","task":"5","amends":"clause","what":"M2 fixes the three cells' values but does not say what a `jev` object whose `magnitude` is not a number buckets as. I read it as bucket 0 (cosmetic): the row carries a `jev` object so M2 counts it in `R`, and bucket 0 is both the reading that claims least and the only choice under which `c0+c1+c2+c3 == R` always holds.","why":"`floor(x + 0.5)` is undefined on a non-number, so some reading had to be chosen for the shape to stay total; the same guard drops non-numeric `compelled`/`plan_fault` out of `k`/`p` while leaving the row in `R`.","id":"01M2Q70JNA000038XTD3Y25567","ts":1789632989866}
{"kind":"driver:amendment","task":"5","amends":"clause","what":"The Context lists the pins that move as the two files' header, row and totals literals. Three further pins in `tests/test_authoring_census_amendments.py` read the same two things by position rather than by literal — `last_cells`/`row_for` taking `split(\"\\t\")[-1]` as the `amendments` cell, and four `endswith(\" amendments=<n>\")` totals assertions — and the three new columns move both. I rewrote those reads to go by name: `AMENDMENTS_FROM_END`, derived from `COLUMN_NAMES`, and a new `totals_field(line, name)` helper. No `def test_` was added or removed; the file still defines exactly 19.","why":"M4 requires that file green on the patched tree with its header and totals pins moved. A positional read of the `amendments` cell is that same pin wearing a different spelling, so moving it is the clause as written; reading by name means the next column to land after these three does not have to touch the file again.","id":"01M2Q70JNA0001PYF16WSK5PYD","ts":1789632989866}
